# Co-install hygiene, mirroring loom's own committed .gitignore: `.squad/` is a
# FOREIGN tool's runtime state directory (a SQLite database -- `squad.db` plus
# its `-wal` / `-shm` companions). Loom neither writes nor reads it; it simply
# materializes in the checkout when that tool runs here. Left unignored it sits
# untracked and visible to this repo's documented `git add -A` Builder step, so
# a binary DB holding another tool's session state can be staged into a remote
# -- and THIS repo is public. Deliberately NOT inherited from loom's
# EPHEMERAL_PATTERNS (see loom's .gitignore: consumer repos have no reason to
# inherit a rule for a tool they may not use), so it is declared here instead.
.squad/

# The CLI's documented default output (`./Zc.mat`, written to the current
# directory when no --zc-mat path is given). Never a tracked file.
Zc.mat
